[
    "The NgramRL system enhances reinforcement learning (RL) post-training by using a rollout-aware n-gram caching mechanism.",
    "This approach addresses the high computational costs of rollout generation during RL post-training, especially in Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO).",
    "NgramRL maintains a per-prompt n-gram cache built from prior rollouts of the same prompt.",
    "The n-gram cache allows proposing draft tokens based on previously generated outputs, leveraging temporal locality of prompts.",
    "Prior rollouts can cover 48-96% of later rollouts across consecutive epochs, indicating significant overlap exploited by NgramRL.",
    "NgramRL operates as a model-free drafter, requiring no additional model training or parameters.",
    "It uses outputs from the policy's own rollouts to populate the n-gram cache, keeping drafts aligned with the evolving policy.",
    "This self-updating mechanism avoids the need for a persistent GPU-resident drafter state.",
    "During each training step, NgramRL proposes draft tokens from the n-gram cache, which are verified by the policy in a single forward pass.",
    "The draft-and-verify procedure preserves the output distribution, maintaining accuracy and convergence.",
    "NgramRL includes an adaptive fan-out prefetcher that speculatively prepares next-step drafts based on likely verification outcomes.",
    "The prefetching mechanism reduces host computation time by overlapping CPU work with GPU processing.",
    "This overlap collapses the decode iteration to GPU busy time, enhancing overall efficiency.",
    "NgramRL commits 3.60-7.77 tokens per target-model forward, up to 1.99 times more than traditional SuffixDecoding methods.",
    "It achieves 7.0 times more tokens per forward than prompt-lookup decoding.",
    "The prefetcher can deliver up to 1.38 times the measured rollout speedup compared to synchronous execution.",
    "NgramRL reduces costs associated with RL post-training while preserving model output accuracy.",
    "NgramRL effectively utilizes n-gram caching to accelerate rollout generation and maintain alignment with the evolving policy.",
    "NgramRL improves computational efficiency through asynchronous prefetching."
] 

