[
    "Hierarchical Collaborative Preference Distillation (HCPD) plays a crucial role in optimizing item preference alignment for enhanced Semantic ID (SID) generation through a structured distillation process.",
    "The primary objective of HCPD is to leverage collaborative preferences from a teacher model to improve the recommendation performance of a student model.",
    "HCPD utilizes a frozen discriminative recommender, specifically DuoRec, as the teacher to provide collaborative preferences over candidate items.",
    "The teacher model is designed to capture user-specific preference differences.",
    "The teacher model reflects the relative relevance of competing candidates based on user interaction history.",
    "The distillation process involves aligning the teacher's conditional preferences over legal next tokens with those of the generator (student model).",
    "This alignment is achieved through the use of conditional KL divergence.",
    "Conditional KL divergence compares the full distributions over all legal next tokens.",
    "Conditional KL divergence provides explicit supervision on inter-item collaborative preferences.",
    "Removing HCPD leads to significant performance degradation across various datasets.",
    "There is a notable drop in Recall@5 by 10.9% to 18.0% when HCPD is removed.",
    "HCPD supplements the positive-item supervision provided by the cross-entropy (CE) objective with collaborative preferences.",
    "Collaborative preferences guide the generation of SIDs.",
    "HCPD is optimized alongside the CE objective.",
    "The joint optimization balances the distillation of collaborative preferences with the observed target distributions.",
    "The joint training enhances the model's ability to prioritize relevant items, particularly at the top of the recommendation list.",
    "Empirical evaluations demonstrate that HCPD consistently outperforms its variant HCPD-Full across multiple metrics.",
    "HCPD particularly outperforms in NDCG@5 and Recall@5 metrics.",
    "HCPD's design effectively prioritizes relevant items and improves overall recommendation quality.",
    "HCPD significantly enhances SID generation by aligning item preferences through a structured distillation process.",
    "HCPD leverages collaborative information from a teacher model to improve the student model's performance in generating relevant recommendations.",
    "HCPD plays a critical role in optimizing item preference alignment.",
    "Optimizing item preference alignment through HCPD leads to better user satisfaction in recommendation systems."
