    "Each codebook family employs distinct approaches to generate representative values for embeddings in low-bit language models.",
    "Uniform codebooks place values at equal intervals between -1 and 1.",
    "With two bits, the uniform codebook values are {-1, -1/3, 1/3, 1}.",
    "There is a zero-centered variant of the uniform codebook called Uniform*.",
    "Uniform* includes zero and uses K - 1 equally spaced values.",
    "The two-bit Uniform* codebook values are {-1, 0, 1}.",
    "Uniform codebooks ensure a straightforward distribution of values across the specified range.",
    "Normal-quantile codebooks place values at quantiles of a standard normal distribution.",
    "Normal-quantile codebooks concentrate more values near zero.",
    "For more than two bits, normal-quantile codebook quantiles are determined at probabilities (k + 1/2)/K for k = 0 to K - 1.",
    "All normal-quantile codebook values are normalized by their largest absolute value.",
    "For two bits, the normal-quantile codebook uses a fixed codebook with values {-1, -0.3186, 0.3186, 1}.",
    "Normal-quantile codebooks are beneficial for capturing the distribution of embeddings centered around zero.",
    "Lloyd-Max codebooks are adaptive and learn values from the distribution of trained embeddings.",
    "Each embedding is normalized initially in Lloyd-Max to prevent magnitude differences from skewing the codebook.",
    "Lloyd-Max codebook values are initialized at quantiles of a sample of normalized components.",
    "Lloyd-Max construction involves assigning sampled components to their nearest codebook value.",
    "Lloyd-Max updates each codebook value to the mean of the assigned components.",
    "The Lloyd-Max process is repeated multiple times, typically 60 iterations.",
    "Lloyd-Max codebooks closely fit the actual distribution of embeddings due to their iterative learning process.",
    "In summary, uniform codebooks use a simple, evenly spaced approach.",
    "Normal-quantile codebooks emphasize values near zero based on a statistical distribution.",
    "Lloyd-Max codebooks adapt to specific characteristics of embeddings through an iterative learning process.",
