Statements:
[
    "PAC-MAN integrates safety and perception constraints for effective humanoid dodgeball evasion through a combination of control barrier functions (CBFs) and perception-aware reinforcement learning (RL).",
    "The framework is designed to enable a humanoid robot to avoid being struck by a ball while maintaining balance, using only limited onboard sensing capabilities.",
    "The PAC-MAN framework utilizes a head-mounted depth camera to perceive the incoming ball.",
    "The robot's policy operates under the constraint that it cannot access the ball's state directly; instead, it must infer information about the ball from depth observations.",
    "This setup models the task as a partially observed Markov decision process, where the robot must react quickly to avoid contact.",
    "Control Barrier Functions (CBFs) are employed to encode safety constraints that ensure the robot avoids collisions.",
    "The framework distinguishes between two types of CBFs: Link-CBF and Joint-CBF.",
    "Link-CBF provides lightweight per-link rewards during training.",
    "Joint-CBF offers a stronger whole-body joint-space projection that can guide training or be used as a runtime filter.",
    "The choice of CBF depends on the quality of the perceptual input.",
    "Joint-CBF performs best with accurate ball state information.",
    "Link-CBF is more suitable for deployment under limited perception.",
    "PAC-MAN incorporates an adversarial motion prior (AMP) to regularize the robot's evasive movements.",
    "The AMP encourages the robot to adopt reflex-like evasive actions such as crouching, leaning, and sidestepping.",
    "The AMP is trained using a discriminator that distinguishes between policy-generated transitions and human-derived motion clips.",
    "The discriminator promotes natural and effective evasive behaviors.",
    "PAC-MAN is trained using Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) across multiple parallel environments.",
    "The robot learns effective evasion strategies in a simulated setting before deployment on a physical robot.",
    "The robot can successfully dodge balls with a high success rate (95%) relying solely on depth perception and proprioception.",
    "The effectiveness of the learned evasive reflexes is closely tied to the quality of the perceptual input.",
    "Usable barrier structures depend on perceptual observability.",
    "Better perception leads to improved safety performance.",
    "PAC-MAN integrates CBFs to ensure collision avoidance.",
    "PAC-MAN employs an AMP to guide natural evasive movements.",
    "The policy is trained under realistic sensory limitations.",
    "This approach allows the humanoid robot to react swiftly and safely in a dynamic environment.",
    "Coupling perception with safety mechanisms is important in robotic applications."
] 

